#: ../../library/turtle.rst:454
msgid ""
">>> turtle.setheading(90)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.setheading(90)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:464
msgid ""
"Move the turtle to the origin, coordinates (0,0). The turtle's heading is "
"set to its start orientation, which depends on the turtle mode, see :func:"
"`mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:475
msgid ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-10.00)\n"
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-10.00)\n"
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:493 ../../library/turtle.rst:1557
msgid "an integer or ``None``"
msgstr "liczba całkowita lub ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:495
msgid ""
"Draw a circle with the given *radius*. The center is *radius* units left of "
"the turtle; *extent*, an angle, determines which part of the circle is "
"drawn. If *extent* is not given, draw the entire circle. If *extent* is not "
"a full circle, one endpoint of the arc is the current pen position. Draw the "
"arc in counterclockwise direction if *radius* is positive, otherwise in "
"clockwise direction. Finally, the turtle's heading is changed by *extent*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:503
msgid ""
"As the circle is approximated by an inscribed regular polygon, *steps* "
"determines the number of steps to use. If not given, it will be calculated "
"automatically. May be used to draw regular polygons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:507
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0\n"
">>> turtle.circle(50)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0\n"
">>> turtle.circle(120, 180)  # draw a semicircle\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,240.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"180.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0\n"
">>> turtle.circle(50)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(-0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0\n"
">>> turtle.circle(120, 180)  # narysuj półkole\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,240.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"180.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:533
msgid "a positive integer or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:534
msgid "a colorstring or a numeric color tuple"
msgstr "colorstring lub numeryczna krotka koloru"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:536
msgid ""
"Draw a circular dot with diameter *size*, using *color*. If *size* is not "
"given, the larger of ``pensize + 4`` and ``2 * pensize`` is used. If *color* "
"is not given, the current pencolor is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:540
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.dot()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50); turtle.dot(20, \"blue\"); turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(100.00,-0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.dot()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50); turtle.dot(20, \"blue\"); turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(100.00,-0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:554
msgid ""
"Stamp a copy of the turtle shape onto the canvas at the current turtle "
"position.  Return a stamp_id for that stamp, which can be used to delete it "
"by calling ``clearstamp(stamp_id)``."
msgstr ""
"Stempluje kopię kształtu żółwia na płótnie w bieżącej pozycji żółwia. Zwraca "
"stamp_id dla tego stempla, który może być użyty do usunięcia go przez "
"wywołanie ``clearstamp(stamp_id)``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:558
msgid ""
">>> turtle.color(\"blue\")\n"
">>> stamp_id = turtle.stamp()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.color(\"blue\")\n"
">>> stamp_id = turtle.stamp()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:568
msgid "an integer, must be return value of previous :func:`stamp` call"
msgstr ""
"liczba całkowita, musi być wartością zwróconą przez wywołanie poprzedniego :"
"func:`stamp`"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:571
msgid "Delete stamp with given *stampid*."
msgstr "Usunięcie stempla z podanym *stampid*."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:573
msgid ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(150.00,-0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.color(\"blue\")\n"
">>> astamp = turtle.stamp()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(200.00,-0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.clearstamp(astamp)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(200.00,-0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(150.00,-0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.color(\"blue\")\n"
">>> astamp = turtle.stamp()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(200.00,-0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.clearstamp(astamp)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(200.00,-0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:590
msgid "an integer (or ``None``)"
msgstr "liczba całkowita (lub ``None``)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:592
msgid ""
"Delete all or first/last *n* of turtle's stamps.  If *n* is ``None``, delete "
"all stamps, if *n* > 0 delete first *n* stamps, else if *n* < 0 delete last "
"*n* stamps."
msgstr ""
"Usuwa wszystkie lub pierwsze/ostatnie *n* stempli żółwia. Jeśli *n* to "
"``None``, usuwa wszystkie stemple, jeśli *n* > 0 usuwa pierwsze *n* stempli, "
"inaczej jeśli *n* < 0 usuwa ostatnie *n* stempli."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:596
msgid ""
">>> for i in range(8):\n"
"...     unused_stamp_id = turtle.stamp()\n"
"...     turtle.fd(30)\n"
">>> turtle.clearstamps(2)\n"
">>> turtle.clearstamps(-2)\n"
">>> turtle.clearstamps()"
msgstr ""
">>> for i in range(8):\n"
"...     unused_stamp_id = turtle.stamp()\n"
"...     turtle.fd(30)\n"
">>> turtle.clearstamps(2)\n"
">>> turtle.clearstamps(-2)\n"
">>> turtle.clearstamps()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:609
msgid ""
"Undo (repeatedly) the last turtle action(s).  Number of available undo "
"actions is determined by the size of the undobuffer."
msgstr ""
"Cofa (wielokrotnie) ostatnią akcję (akcje) żółwia. Liczba dostępnych cofnięć "
"zależy od rozmiaru bufora cofania."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:612
msgid ""
">>> for i in range(4):\n"
"...     turtle.fd(50); turtle.lt(80)\n"
"...\n"
">>> for i in range(8):\n"
"...     turtle.undo()"
msgstr ""
">>> for i in range(4):\n"
"...     turtle.fd(50); turtle.lt(80)\n"
"...\n"
">>> for i in range(8):\n"
"...     turtle.undo()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:624
msgid "an integer, a string or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:626
msgid ""
"Return or set the turtle's speed. If *speed* is not given, return the "
"current speed. Otherwise set the turtle's speed to an integer from 0 to 10. "
"If *speed* is a number greater than 10 or smaller than 0.5, the speed is set "
"to 0. You can also use these names instead of numbers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:631
msgid "\"fastest\": 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:632
msgid "\"fast\": 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:633
msgid "\"normal\": 6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:634
msgid "\"slow\": 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:635
msgid "\"slowest\": 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:637
msgid ""
"Speeds from 1 to 10 give increasingly faster animation of line drawing and "
"turtle turning. A speed of 0 means that no animation takes place: :func:"
"`forward` and :func:`back` make the turtle jump, and likewise :func:`left` "
"and :func:`right` make the turtle turn instantly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:642
msgid ""
">>> turtle.speed()\n"
"3\n"
">>> turtle.speed('normal')\n"
">>> turtle.speed()\n"
"6\n"
">>> turtle.speed(9)\n"
">>> turtle.speed()\n"
"9"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.speed()\n"
"3\n"
">>> turtle.speed('normal')\n"
">>> turtle.speed()\n"
"6\n"
">>> turtle.speed(9)\n"
">>> turtle.speed()\n"
"9"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:656
msgid "Tell Turtle's state"
msgstr "Pobieranie stanu żółwia"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:661
msgid "Return the turtle's current location (x,y) as a :class:`Vec2D` vector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:663
msgid ""
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(440.00,-0.00)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(440.00,-0.00)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:672 ../../library/turtle.rst:737
msgid "a number or a pair/vector of numbers or a turtle instance"
msgstr "liczba lub para/wektor liczb lub instancja żółwia"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:673 ../../library/turtle.rst:738
msgid "a number if *x* is a number, else ``None``"
msgstr "liczba, jeśli *x* jest liczbą, w przeciwnym razie ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:675
msgid ""
"Return the angle of the line from the turtle's position to (x,y). If *y* is "
"``None``, *x* must be a pair of coordinates, a :class:`Vec2D`, for example "
"as returned by :func:`pos`, or another turtle. The angle is measured from "
"the turtle's start orientation, which depends on the turtle mode, see :func:"
"`mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:681
msgid ""
">>> turtle.goto(10, 10)\n"
">>> turtle.towards(0,0)\n"
"225.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.goto(10, 10)\n"
">>> turtle.towards(0,0)\n"
"225.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:691
msgid "Return the turtle's x coordinate."
msgstr "Zwraca współrzędną x żółwia."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:693
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(50)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(64.28,76.60)\n"
">>> print(round(turtle.xcor(), 5))\n"
"64.27876"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(50)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> turtle.pos()\n"
"(64.28,76.60)\n"
">>> print(round(turtle.xcor(), 5))\n"
"64.27876"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:707
msgid "Return the turtle's y coordinate."
msgstr "Zwraca współrzędną y żółwia."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:709
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> print(turtle.pos())\n"
"(50.00,86.60)\n"
">>> print(round(turtle.ycor(), 5))\n"
"86.60254"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.forward(100)\n"
">>> print(turtle.pos())\n"
"(50.00,86.60)\n"
">>> print(round(turtle.ycor(), 5))\n"
"86.60254"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:723
msgid ""
"Return the turtle's current heading. The value depends on the turtle mode, "
"see :func:`mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:726
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(67)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(67)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"67.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:740
msgid ""
"Return the distance from the turtle to (x,y) in turtle step units. If *y* is "
"``None``, *x* must be a pair of coordinates, a :class:`Vec2D`, for example "
"as returned by :func:`pos`, or another turtle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:744
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.distance(30,40)\n"
"50.0\n"
">>> turtle.distance((30,40))\n"
"50.0\n"
">>> joe = Turtle()\n"
">>> joe.forward(77)\n"
">>> turtle.distance(joe)\n"
"77.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.distance(30,40)\n"
"50.0\n"
">>> turtle.distance((30,40))\n"
"50.0\n"
">>> joe = Turtle()\n"
">>> joe.forward(77)\n"
">>> turtle.distance(joe)\n"
"77.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:759
msgid "Settings for measurement"
msgstr "Ustawienia pomiarowe"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:765
msgid ""
"Set the angle measurement units to degrees. The number of degrees in a full "
"circle is set to *fullcircle*, which defaults to 360."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:768
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(90)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0\n"
"\n"
">>> # Change angle measurement unit to grad (also known as gon,\n"
">>> # grade, or gradian and equals 1/100-th of the right angle.)\n"
">>> turtle.degrees(400.0)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"100.0\n"
">>> turtle.degrees(360)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(90)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0\n"
"\n"
">>> # Zmień jednostkę miary kąta na grad (inaczej gon\n"
">>> # lub gradus; jest on równy 1/100 kąta prostego).\n"
">>> turtle.degrees(400.0)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"100.0\n"
">>> turtle.degrees(360)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:788
msgid ""
"Set the angle measurement units to radians.  Equivalent to ``degrees(2 * "
"math.pi)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:791
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(90)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0\n"
">>> turtle.radians()\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"1.5707963267948966"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.left(90)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"90.0\n"
">>> turtle.radians()\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"1.5707963267948966"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:813
msgid "Drawing state"
msgstr "Stan rysowania"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:819
msgid "Lower the pen. The turtle draws a line when it moves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:826
msgid "Lift the pen. The turtle does not draw when it moves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:832 ../../library/turtle.rst:1249
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1250 ../../library/turtle.rst:1251
msgid "a positive number or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:834
msgid ""
"Return or set the line thickness. If *width* is not given, return the "
"current pensize. If resizemode is set to \"auto\" and the turtle shape is a "
"polygon, that polygon is drawn with the same line thickness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:838
msgid ""
">>> turtle.pensize()\n"
"1\n"
">>> turtle.pensize(10)   # from here on lines of width 10 are drawn"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.pensize()\n"
"1\n"
">>> turtle.pensize(10)   # od tego momentu rysowane są linie o szerokości 10"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:848
msgid "a dictionary with some or all of the below listed keys"
msgstr "słownik z niektórymi lub wszystkimi z poniższych kluczy"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:849
msgid "one or more keyword-arguments with the below listed keys as keywords"
msgstr ""
"jedno lub więcej argumentów nazwanych z poniższymi kluczami jako nazwami"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:851
msgid ""
"Return or set the pen's attributes in a \"pen-dictionary\" with the "
"following key/value pairs:"
msgstr ""
"Zwraca lub ustawia atrybuty pióra w „pióro-słowniku” z następującymi parami "
"klucz/wartość:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:854
msgid "\"shown\": True/False"
msgstr "„shown”: True/False"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:855
msgid "\"pendown\": True/False"
msgstr "„pendown”: True/False"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:856
msgid "\"pencolor\": color-string or color-tuple"
msgstr "„pencolor”: nazwa koloru (color-string) lub kolor-krotka"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:857
msgid "\"fillcolor\": color-string or color-tuple"
msgstr "„fillcolor”: nazwa koloru (color-string) lub kolor-krotka"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:858
msgid "\"pensize\": positive number"
msgstr "„pensize”: liczba dodatnia"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:859
msgid "\"speed\": number in range 0..10"
msgstr "„speed”: liczba z przedziału 0..10"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:860
msgid "\"resizemode\": \"auto\" or \"user\" or \"noresize\""
msgstr "„resizemode”: „auto” lub „user” lub „noresize”"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:861
msgid "\"stretchfactor\": (positive number, positive number)"
msgstr "„stretchfactor”: (liczba dodatnia, liczba dodatnia)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:862
msgid "\"outline\": positive number"
msgstr "„outline”: liczba dodatnia"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:863
msgid "\"tilt\": number"
msgstr "„tilt”: liczba"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:865
msgid ""
"This dictionary can be used as argument for a subsequent call to :func:`pen` "
"to restore the former pen-state.  Moreover one or more of these attributes "
"can be provided as keyword-arguments.  This can be used to set several pen "
"attributes in one statement."
msgstr ""
"Ten słownik może być użyty jako argument dla kolejnego wywołania :func:`pen` "
"w celu przywrócenia poprzedniego stanu pióra. Co więcej, jeden lub więcej z "
"tych atrybutów może być przekazany jako argument nazwany. Można to "
"wykorzystać do ustawienia kilku atrybutów pióra w jednej instrukcji."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:870
msgid ""
">>> turtle.pen(fillcolor=\"black\", pencolor=\"red\", pensize=10)\n"
">>> sorted(turtle.pen().items())\n"
"[('fillcolor', 'black'), ('outline', 1), ('pencolor', 'red'),\n"
" ('pendown', True), ('pensize', 10), ('resizemode', 'noresize'),\n"
" ('shearfactor', 0.0), ('shown', True), ('speed', 9),\n"
" ('stretchfactor', (1.0, 1.0)), ('tilt', 0.0)]\n"
">>> penstate=turtle.pen()\n"
">>> turtle.color(\"yellow\", \"\")\n"
">>> turtle.penup()\n"
">>> sorted(turtle.pen().items())[:3]\n"
"[('fillcolor', ''), ('outline', 1), ('pencolor', 'yellow')]\n"
">>> turtle.pen(penstate, fillcolor=\"green\")\n"
">>> sorted(turtle.pen().items())[:3]\n"
"[('fillcolor', 'green'), ('outline', 1), ('pencolor', 'red')]"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.pen(fillcolor=\"black\", pencolor=\"red\", pensize=10)\n"
">>> sorted(turtle.pen().items())\n"
"[('fillcolor', 'black'), ('outline', 1), ('pencolor', 'red'),\n"
" ('pendown', True), ('pensize', 10), ('resizemode', 'noresize'),\n"
" ('shearfactor', 0.0), ('shown', True), ('speed', 9),\n"
" ('stretchfactor', (1.0, 1.0)), ('tilt', 0.0)]\n"
">>> penstate=turtle.pen()\n"
">>> turtle.color(\"yellow\", \"\")\n"
">>> turtle.penup()\n"
">>> sorted(turtle.pen().items())[:3]\n"
"[('fillcolor', ''), ('outline', 1), ('pencolor', 'yellow')]\n"
">>> turtle.pen(penstate, fillcolor=\"green\")\n"
">>> sorted(turtle.pen().items())[:3]\n"
"[('fillcolor', 'green'), ('outline', 1), ('pencolor', 'red')]"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:891
msgid "Return ``True`` if the pen is down, ``False`` if it's up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:893
msgid ""
">>> turtle.penup()\n"
">>> turtle.isdown()\n"
"False\n"
">>> turtle.pendown()\n"
">>> turtle.isdown()\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.penup()\n"
">>> turtle.isdown()\n"
"False\n"
">>> turtle.pendown()\n"
">>> turtle.isdown()\n"
"True"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:905
msgid "Color control"
msgstr "Kontrola koloru"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:911
msgid "Return or set the pencolor."
msgstr "Zwraca lub ustawia kolor pióra."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:913 ../../library/turtle.rst:965
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1606
msgid "Four input formats are allowed:"
msgstr "Dozwolone są cztery formaty wejściowe:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:915
msgid "``pencolor()``"
msgstr "``pencolor()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:916
msgid ""
"Return the current pencolor as color specification string or as a tuple (see "
"example).  May be used as input to another :func:`color`, :func:`pencolor`, :"
"func:`fillcolor` or :func:`bgcolor` call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:921
msgid "``pencolor(colorstring)``"
msgstr "``pencolor(colorstring)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:922
msgid ""
"Set the pencolor to *colorstring*, which is a Tk color specification string, "
"such as ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"``, or ``\"#33cc8c\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:925
msgid "``pencolor((r, g, b))``"
msgstr "``pencolor((r, g, b))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:926
msgid ""
"Set the pencolor to the RGB color represented by the tuple of *r*, *g*, and "
"*b*. Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode, where "
"colormode is either 1.0 or 255 (see :func:`colormode`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:930
msgid "``pencolor(r, g, b)``"
msgstr "``pencolor(r, g, b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:931
msgid ""
"Set the pencolor to the RGB color represented by *r*, *g*, and *b*. Each of "
"*r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:934
msgid ""
"If the turtle shape is a polygon, the outline of that polygon is drawn with "
"the newly set pencolor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:937
msgid ""
">>> colormode()\n"
"1.0\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"'red'\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(\"brown\")\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"'brown'\n"
">>> tup = (0.2, 0.8, 0.55)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(tup)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(0.2, 0.8, 0.5490196078431373)\n"
">>> colormode(255)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(51.0, 204.0, 140.0)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor('#32c18f')\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> colormode()\n"
"1.0\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"'red'\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(\"brown\")\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"'brown'\n"
">>> tup = (0.2, 0.8, 0.55)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor(tup)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(0.2, 0.8, 0.5490196078431373)\n"
">>> colormode(255)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(51.0, 204.0, 140.0)\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor('#32c18f')\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:963
msgid "Return or set the fillcolor."
msgstr "Zwraca lub ustawia kolor wypełnienia."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:967
msgid "``fillcolor()``"
msgstr "``fillcolor()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:968
msgid ""
"Return the current fillcolor as color specification string, possibly in "
"tuple format (see example).  May be used as input to another :func:`color`, :"
"func:`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` or :func:`bgcolor` call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:973
msgid "``fillcolor(colorstring)``"
msgstr "``fillcolor(colorstring)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:974
msgid ""
"Set the fillcolor to *colorstring*, which is a Tk color specification "
"string, such as ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"``, or ``\"#33cc8c\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:977
msgid "``fillcolor((r, g, b))``"
msgstr "``fillcolor((r, g, b))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:978
msgid ""
"Set the fillcolor to the RGB color represented by the tuple of *r*, *g*, and "
"*b*. Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode, where "
"colormode is either 1.0 or 255 (see :func:`colormode`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:982
msgid "``fillcolor(r, g, b)``"
msgstr "``fillcolor(r, g, b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:983
msgid ""
"Set the fillcolor to the RGB color represented by *r*, *g*, and *b*. Each of "
"*r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:986
msgid ""
"If the turtle shape is a polygon, the interior of that polygon is drawn with "
"the newly set fillcolor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:989
msgid ""
">>> turtle.fillcolor(\"violet\")\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"'violet'\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor((50, 193, 143))  # Integers, not floats\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor('#ffffff')\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"(255.0, 255.0, 255.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.fillcolor(\"violet\")\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"'violet'\n"
">>> turtle.pencolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor((50, 193, 143))  # całkowite, nie zmiennoprzecinkowe\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"(50.0, 193.0, 143.0)\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor('#ffffff')\n"
">>> turtle.fillcolor()\n"
"(255.0, 255.0, 255.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1010
msgid "Return or set the pencolor and fillcolor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1012
msgid ""
"Several input formats are allowed. They use 0 to 3 arguments as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1015
msgid "``color()``"
msgstr "``color()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1016
msgid ""
"Return the current pencolor and the current fillcolor as a pair of color "
"specification strings or tuples as returned by :func:`pencolor` and :func:"
"`fillcolor`."
msgstr ""
"Zwraca bieżący kolor pióra i bieżący kolor wypełnienia jako parę ciągów "
"specyfikacji kolorów lub krotek zwracanych przez :func:`pencolor` i :func:"
"`fillcolor`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1020
msgid "``color(colorstring)``, ``color((r,g,b))``, ``color(r,g,b)``"
msgstr "``color(colorstring)``, ``color((r,g,b))``, ``color(r,g,b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1021
msgid ""
"Inputs as in :func:`pencolor`. Set both the pencolor and the fillcolor to "
"the given value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1024
msgid ""
"``color(colorstring1, colorstring2)``, ``color((r1,g1,b1), (r2,g2,b2))``"
msgstr ""
"``color(colorstring1, colorstring2)``, ``color((r1,g1,b1), (r2,g2,b2))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1025
msgid ""
"Equivalent to ``pencolor(colorstring1)`` and ``fillcolor(colorstring2)`` and "
"analogously if the other input format is used."
msgstr ""
"Odpowiednik dla ``pencolor(colorstring1)`` i ``fillcolor(colorstring2)`` "
"oraz analogicznie, jeśli używany jest inny format wejścia."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1028
msgid ""
"If the turtle shape is a polygon, the outline and interior of that polygon "
"are drawn with the newly set colors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1031
msgid ""
">>> turtle.color(\"red\", \"green\")\n"
">>> turtle.color()\n"
"('red', 'green')\n"
">>> color(\"#285078\", \"#a0c8f0\")\n"
">>> color()\n"
"((40.0, 80.0, 120.0), (160.0, 200.0, 240.0))"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.color(\"red\", \"green\")\n"
">>> turtle.color()\n"
"('red', 'green')\n"
">>> color(\"#285078\", \"#a0c8f0\")\n"
">>> color()\n"
"((40.0, 80.0, 120.0), (160.0, 200.0, 240.0))"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1042
msgid "See also: Screen method :func:`colormode`."
msgstr "Zobacz także: Metoda klasy Screen :func:`colormode`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1046
msgid "Filling"
msgstr "Wypełnienie"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1056
msgid "Return ``True`` if the turtle is filling, ``False`` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1058
msgid ""
">>> turtle.begin_fill()\n"
">>> if turtle.filling():\n"
"...    turtle.pensize(5)\n"
"... else:\n"
"...    turtle.pensize(3)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.begin_fill()\n"
">>> if turtle.filling():\n"
"...    turtle.pensize(5)\n"
"... else:\n"
"...    turtle.pensize(3)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1069
msgid "Fill the shape drawn in the ``with turtle.fill():`` block."
msgstr "Wypełnij kształt narysowany w bloku ``with turtle.fill():``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1071
msgid ""
">>> turtle.color(\"black\", \"red\")\n"
">>> with turtle.fill():\n"
"...     turtle.circle(80)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.color(\"black\", \"red\")\n"
">>> with turtle.fill():\n"
"...     turtle.circle(80)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1078
msgid ""
"Using :func:`!fill` is equivalent to adding the :func:`begin_fill` before "
"the fill-block and :func:`end_fill` after the fill-block:"
msgstr ""
"Użycie :func:`!fill` jest równoznaczne z dodaniem :func:`begin_fill` przed "
"blokiem wypełnienia i :func:`end_fill` po bloku wypełnienia:"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1081 ../../library/turtle.rst:1106
msgid ""
">>> turtle.color(\"black\", \"red\")\n"
">>> turtle.begin_fill()\n"
">>> turtle.circle(80)\n"
">>> turtle.end_fill()"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.color(\"black\", \"red\")\n"
">>> turtle.begin_fill()\n"
">>> turtle.circle(80)\n"
">>> turtle.end_fill()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1094
msgid "To be called just before drawing a shape to be filled."
msgstr "Do wywołania tuż przed rysowaniem kształtu do wypełnienia."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1099
msgid "Fill the shape drawn after the last call to :func:`begin_fill`."
msgstr "Wypełnia kształt narysowany po ostatnim wywołaniu :func:`begin_fill`."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1101
msgid ""
"Whether or not overlap regions for self-intersecting polygons or multiple "
"shapes are filled depends on the operating system graphics, type of overlap, "
"and number of overlaps.  For example, the Turtle star above may be either "
"all yellow or have some white regions."
msgstr ""
"To, czy obszary nakładania się przecinających się wielokątów lub wielu "
"kształtów są wypełnione, zależy od grafiki systemu operacyjnego, typu "
"nakładania się i liczby nakładających się obszarów.  Na przykład żółwiowa "
"gwiazda na górze rozdziału może być cała żółta lub mieć kilka białych "
"obszarów."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1116
msgid "More drawing control"
msgstr "Więcej kontroli rysowania"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1120
msgid ""
"Delete the turtle's drawings and re-center the turtle. The turtle's settings "
"are restored to their default values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1123
msgid ""
">>> turtle.goto(0,-22)\n"
">>> turtle.left(100)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-22.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"100.0\n"
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.goto(0,-22)\n"
">>> turtle.left(100)\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,-22.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"100.0\n"
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.position()\n"
"(0.00,0.00)\n"
">>> turtle.heading()\n"
"0.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1141
msgid ""
"Delete the turtle's drawings from the screen. The state and position of the "
"turtle as well as the drawings of other turtles are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1147
msgid "object to be written to the TurtleScreen"
msgstr "obiekt, który ma zostać zapisany na TurtleScreen"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1148
msgid "True/False"
msgstr "True/False"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1149
msgid "one of the strings \"left\", \"center\" or right\""
msgstr "jedna z wartości „left”, „center” lub „right”"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1150
msgid "a triple (fontname, fontsize, fonttype)"
msgstr "trójka wartości (fontname, fontsize, fonttype)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1152
msgid ""
"Write text - the string representation of *arg* - at the current turtle "
"position according to *align* (\"left\", \"center\" or \"right\") and with "
"the given font.  If *move* is true, the pen is moved to the bottom-right "
"corner of the text.  By default, *move* is ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Pisze tekst – reprezentację obiektu *arg* – w bieżącej pozycji żółwia "
"zgodnie z *align* (\"left\", \"center\" lub \"right\") i z podaną czcionką.  "
"Jeśli *move* to ``True``, pióro jest przesuwane do prawego dolnego rogu "
"tekstu.  Domyślnie *move* ma wartość ``False``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1157
msgid ""
">>> turtle.write(\"Home = \", True, align=\"center\")\n"
">>> turtle.write((0,0), True)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.write(\"początek = \", True, align=\"center\")\n"
">>> turtle.write((0,0), True)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1165
msgid "Turtle state"
msgstr "Stan żółwia"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1168
msgid "Visibility"
msgstr "Widoczność"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1173
msgid "Make the turtle invisible. If the pen is down, movement still draws."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1179
msgid "Make the turtle visible."
msgstr "Sprawia, że żółw jest widoczny."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1184
msgid "Return ``True`` if the turtle is visible, ``False`` if it's hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1186
msgid ""
">>> turtle.hideturtle()\n"
">>> turtle.isvisible()\n"
"False\n"
">>> turtle.showturtle()\n"
">>> turtle.isvisible()\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.hideturtle()\n"
">>> turtle.isvisible()\n"
"False\n"
">>> turtle.showturtle()\n"
">>> turtle.isvisible()\n"
"True"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1198
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr "Wygląd"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1202 ../../library/turtle.rst:1222
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1960
msgid "a string or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1204
msgid ""
"Set the turtle shape to the named shape. If *name* is not given, return the "
"name of the current shape. The shape must exist in the :class:"
"`TurtleScreen`'s shape dictionary. Initially there are the following shapes: "
"\"arrow\", \"turtle\", \"circle\", \"square\", \"triangle\" and \"classic\". "
"To add shapes, see the :class:`Screen` method :func:`register_shape`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1210
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'classic'\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"turtle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'turtle'"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'classic'\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"turtle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shape()\n"
"'turtle'"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1224
msgid ""
"Set the resizemode to \"auto\", \"user\" or \"noresize\". If *rmode* is not "
"given, return the current resizemode. The different resizemodes have the "
"following effects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1228
msgid ""
"\"auto\": the turtle is resized according to the value of :func:`pensize`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1229
msgid ""
"\"user\": the turtle is resized according to the stretch factors and outline "
"width, which are set by :func:`shapesize`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1231
msgid "\"noresize\": the turtle is not resized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1233
msgid ""
"``resizemode(\"user\")`` is called by :func:`shapesize` when used with "
"arguments."
msgstr ""
"``resizemode(\"user\")`` jest wywoływana przez :func:`shapesize`, gdy jest "
"użyte z argumentami."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1236
msgid ""
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'noresize'\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"auto\")\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'auto'"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'noresize'\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"auto\")\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode()\n"
"'auto'"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1253
msgid ""
"Return or set the turtle's stretch factors and outline width. If no "
"arguments are given, return the current values. Otherwise set resizemode to "
"\"user\", so that the turtle is displayed stretched according to its stretch "
"factors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1258
msgid "*stretch_wid*: the stretch factor perpendicular to the turtle's heading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1259
msgid ""
"*stretch_len*: the stretch factor in the direction of the turtle's heading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1261
msgid "*outline*: the width of the shape's outline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1263
msgid ""
"For example, ``shapesize(2, 1)`` makes the turtle twice as wide without "
"changing its length. If only *stretch_wid* is given, *stretch_len* is set to "
"the same value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1267
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(1.0, 1.0, 1)\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"user\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(outline=8)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 8)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(1.0, 1.0, 1)\n"
">>> turtle.resizemode(\"user\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 12)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(outline=8)\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize()\n"
"(5, 5, 8)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1283
msgid "number (optional)"
msgstr "liczba (opcjonalna)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1285
msgid ""
"Set or return the current shearfactor. Shear the turtleshape according to "
"the given shearfactor shear, which is the tangent of the shear angle. Do "
"*not* change the turtle's heading (direction of movement). If shear is not "
"given: return the current shearfactor, i. e. the tangent of the shear angle, "
"by which lines parallel to the heading of the turtle are sheared."
msgstr ""
"Ustawia lub zwraca bieżący współczynnik odchylenia. Odchyla kształt żółwia "
"zgodnie z podanym współczynnikiem, który jest tangensem kąta odchylenia. Nie "
"*zmienia* kursu żółwia (kierunku ruchu). Jeśli nie podano współczynnika: "
"zwraca aktualny współczynnik odchylenia, tj. tangens kąta odchylenia, o "
"który odchylają się linie równoległe do kierunku ruchu żółwia."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1292
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor()\n"
"0.5"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor()\n"
"0.5"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1306
msgid ""
"Rotate the turtleshape by *angle* from its current tilt-angle, but do *not* "
"change the turtle's heading (direction of movement)."
msgstr ""
"Obraca żółwia o *kąt* w stosunku do jego aktualnego kąta nachylenia, ale "
"*nie* zmienia jego kursu (kierunku ruchu)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1309
msgid ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(30)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1323 ../../library/turtle.rst:1346
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1347 ../../library/turtle.rst:1348
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1349
msgid "a number (optional)"
msgstr "liczba (opcjonalna)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1325
msgid ""
"Set or return the current tilt-angle. If angle is given, rotate the "
"turtleshape to point in the direction specified by angle, regardless of its "
"current tilt-angle. Do *not* change the turtle's heading (direction of "
"movement). If angle is not given: return the current tilt-angle, i. e. the "
"angle between the orientation of the turtleshape and the heading of the "
"turtle (its direction of movement)."
msgstr ""
"Ustawia lub zwraca bieżący kąt nachylenia. Jeśli podano kąt, obraca żółwia "
"tak, aby wskazywał kierunek określony przez kąt, niezależnie od jego "
"aktualnego kąta nachylenia. Nie *zmienia* kierunku żółwia (kierunku ruchu). "
"Jeśli nie podano kąta: zwraca aktualny kąt nachylenia, tj. kąt między "
"orientacją kształtu żółwia a jego kursem (kierunkiem ruchu)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1333
msgid ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(45)\n"
">>> turtle.tiltangle()\n"
"45.0"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.reset()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"circle\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(5,2)\n"
">>> turtle.tilt(45)\n"
">>> turtle.tiltangle()\n"
"45.0"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1351
msgid "Set or return the current transformation matrix of the turtle shape."
msgstr "Ustawia lub zwraca bieżącą macierz transformacji kształtu żółwia."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1353
msgid ""
"If none of the matrix elements are given, return the transformation matrix "
"as a tuple of 4 elements. Otherwise set the given elements and transform the "
"turtleshape according to the matrix consisting of first row t11, t12 and "
"second row t21, t22. The determinant t11 * t22 - t12 * t21 must not be zero, "
"otherwise an error is raised. Modify stretchfactor, shearfactor and "
"tiltangle according to the given matrix."
msgstr ""
"Jeśli nie podano żadnego z elementów macierzy, zwraca macierz transformacji "
"jako krotkę 4 elementów. W przeciwnym razie ustawia podane elementy i "
"przekształca kształt żółwia zgodnie z macierzą składającą się z pierwszego "
"wiersza t11, t12 i drugiego wiersza t21, t22. Wyznacznik t11 * t22 - t12 * "
"t21 nie może być równy zero, w przeciwnym razie zostanie rzucony błąd. "
"Modyfikuje stretchfactor, shearfactor i tiltangle zgodnie z podaną macierzą."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1362
msgid ""
">>> turtle = Turtle()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(4,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(-0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform()\n"
"(4.0, -1.0, -0.0, 2.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle = Turtle()\n"
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapesize(4,2)\n"
">>> turtle.shearfactor(-0.5)\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform()\n"
"(4.0, -1.0, -0.0, 2.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1375
msgid ""
"Return the current shape polygon as tuple of coordinate pairs. This can be "
"used to define a new shape or components of a compound shape."
msgstr ""
"Zwraca bieżący wielokąt kształtu jako krotkę par współrzędnych. Może to być "
"wykorzystane do zdefiniowania nowego kształtu lub komponentów kształtu "
"złożonego."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1378
msgid ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform(4, -1, 0, 2)\n"
">>> turtle.get_shapepoly()\n"
"((50, -20), (30, 20), (-50, 20), (-30, -20))"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.shape(\"square\")\n"
">>> turtle.shapetransform(4, -1, 0, 2)\n"
">>> turtle.get_shapepoly()\n"
"((50, -20), (30, 20), (-50, 20), (-30, -20))"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1388
msgid "Using events"
msgstr "Korzystanie ze zdarzeń"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1393 ../../library/turtle.rst:1866
msgid "a function with two arguments or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1394 ../../library/turtle.rst:1867
msgid "an integer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1395 ../../library/turtle.rst:1868
msgid "a boolean or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1397
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-click events on this turtle. *fun* is called with the "
"coordinates of the clicked point on the canvas. If *fun* is ``None``, "
"existing bindings are removed. *btn* is the number of the mouse button and "
"defaults to 1, the left mouse button. If *add* is ``True``, a new binding is "
"added, otherwise it replaces a former binding. Example for the anonymous "
"turtle, that is, the procedural way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1404
msgid ""
">>> def turn(x, y):\n"
"...     left(180)\n"
"...\n"
">>> onclick(turn)  # Now clicking into the turtle will turn it.\n"
">>> onclick(None)  # event-binding will be removed"
msgstr ""
">>> def turn(x, y):\n"
"...     left(180)\n"
"...\n"
">>> onclick(turn)  # Teraz kliknięcie w żółwia spowoduje jego obrócenie.\n"
">>> onclick(None)  # powiązanie zdarzenia zostanie usunięte"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1416 ../../library/turtle.rst:1441
msgid ""
"a function with two arguments which will be called with the coordinates of "
"the clicked point on the canvas"
msgstr ""
"funkcja z dwoma argumentami, która zostanie wywołana ze współrzędnymi "
"klikniętego punktu na płótnie"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1418 ../../library/turtle.rst:1443
msgid "number of the mouse-button, defaults to 1 (left mouse button)"
msgstr "numer przycisku myszy, domyślnie 1 (lewy przycisk myszy)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1419 ../../library/turtle.rst:1444
msgid ""
"``True`` or ``False`` -- if ``True``, a new binding will be added, otherwise "
"it will replace a former binding"
msgstr ""
"``True`` lub ``False`` -- jeśli ``True``, zostanie dodane nowe powiązanie, w "
"przeciwnym razie zastąpi poprzednie powiązanie"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1422
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-button-release events on this turtle.  If *fun* is "
"``None``, existing bindings are removed."
msgstr ""
"Wiąże *fun* ze zdarzeniami zwolnienia przycisku myszy na tym żółwiu. Jeśli "
"*fun* to ``None``, istniejące powiązania są usuwane."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1425
msgid ""
">>> class MyTurtle(Turtle):\n"
"...     def glow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"red\")\n"
"...     def unglow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"\")\n"
"...\n"
">>> turtle = MyTurtle()\n"
">>> turtle.onclick(turtle.glow)     # clicking on turtle turns fillcolor "
"red,\n"
">>> turtle.onrelease(turtle.unglow) # releasing turns it to transparent."
msgstr ""
">>> class MyTurtle(Turtle):\n"
"...     def glow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"red\")\n"
"...     def unglow(self,x,y):\n"
"...         self.fillcolor(\"\")\n"
"...\n"
">>> turtle = MyTurtle()\n"
">>> turtle.onclick(turtle.glow)  # kliknięcie na żółwia zmienia fillcolor na "
"czerwony,\n"
">>> turtle.onrelease(turtle.unglow)  # zwolnienie zmienia kolor na "
"przezroczysty."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1447
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to mouse-move events on this turtle.  If *fun* is ``None``, "
"existing bindings are removed."
msgstr ""
"Wiąże *fun* ze zdarzeniami ruchu myszy na tym żółwiu. Jeśli *fun* to "
"``None``, istniejące powiązania są usuwane."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1450
msgid ""
"Remark: Every sequence of mouse-move-events on a turtle is preceded by a "
"mouse-click event on that turtle."
msgstr ""
"Uwaga: Każda sekwencja zdarzeń ruchu myszą na żółwiu jest poprzedzona "
"zdarzeniem kliknięcia myszą na tym żółwiu."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1453
msgid ">>> turtle.ondrag(turtle.goto)"
msgstr ">>> turtle.ondrag(turtle.goto)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1458
msgid ""
"Subsequently, clicking and dragging the Turtle will move it across the "
"screen thereby producing handdrawings (if pen is down)."
msgstr ""
"Następnie kliknięcie i przeciągnięcie żółwia spowoduje przesunięcie go po "
"ekranie, tworząc rysunki odręczne (jeśli pióro jest opuszczone)."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1463
msgid "Special Turtle methods"
msgstr "Specjalne metody żółwi"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1467
msgid ""
"Record the vertices of a polygon drawn in the ``with turtle.poly():`` block. "
"The first and last vertices will be connected."
msgstr ""
"Zapisuje wierzchołki wielokąta narysowanego w bloku ``with turtle.poly():``. "
"Pierwszy i ostatni wierzchołek będą połączone."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1470
msgid ""
">>> with turtle.poly():\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)\n"
"...     turtle.right(60)\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)"
msgstr ""
">>> with turtle.poly():\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)\n"
"...     turtle.right(60)\n"
"...     turtle.forward(100)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1483
msgid ""
"Start recording the vertices of a polygon. The current turtle position is "
"the first vertex of the polygon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1489
msgid ""
"Stop recording the vertices of a polygon. The current turtle position is the "
"last vertex of the polygon. This will be connected with the first vertex."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1495
msgid "Return the last recorded polygon."
msgstr "Zwraca ostatni zarejestrowany wielokąt."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1497
msgid ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.begin_poly()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(100)\n"
">>> turtle.left(20)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(30)\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.end_poly()\n"
">>> p = turtle.get_poly()\n"
">>> register_shape(\"myFavouriteShape\", p)"
msgstr ""
">>> turtle.home()\n"
">>> turtle.begin_poly()\n"
">>> turtle.fd(100)\n"
">>> turtle.left(20)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(30)\n"
">>> turtle.left(60)\n"
">>> turtle.fd(50)\n"
">>> turtle.end_poly()\n"
">>> p = turtle.get_poly()\n"
">>> register_shape(\"mójUlubionyKształt\", p)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1514
msgid ""
"Create and return a clone of the turtle. The clone has the same position, "
"heading and turtle properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1517
msgid ""
">>> leonel = Turtle()\n"
">>> marco = leonel.clone()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1527
msgid "Return the Turtle object itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1529
msgid ""
"Call ``getturtle()`` to get the turtle used by functions such as :func:"
"`forward` and :func:`left`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1532
msgid ""
">>> pet = getturtle()\n"
">>> pet.fd(50)\n"
">>> pet\n"
"<turtle.Turtle object at 0x...>"
msgstr ""
">>> pet = getturtle()\n"
">>> pet.fd(50)\n"
">>> pet\n"
"<turtle.Turtle object at 0x...>"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1543
msgid ""
"Return the :class:`TurtleScreen` object the turtle is drawing on. "
"TurtleScreen methods can then be called for that object."
msgstr ""
"Zwraca obiekt :class:`TurtleScreen`, na którym żółw rysuje. Następnie można "
"wywoływać metody TurtleScreen na tym obiekcie."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1546
msgid ""
">>> ts = turtle.getscreen()\n"
">>> ts\n"
"<turtle._Screen object at 0x...>\n"
">>> ts.bgcolor(\"pink\")"
msgstr ""
">>> ts = turtle.getscreen()\n"
">>> ts\n"
"<turtle._Screen object at 0x...>\n"
">>> ts.bgcolor(\"pink\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1559
msgid ""
"Set or disable the undo buffer. If *size* is an integer, an empty undo "
"buffer of the given size is installed. *size* is the maximum number of "
"turtle actions that can be undone by :func:`undo`. If *size* is ``None``, "
"the undo buffer is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1564
msgid ">>> turtle.setundobuffer(42)"
msgstr ">>> turtle.setundobuffer(42)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1572
msgid "Return the number of entries in the undo buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1574
msgid ""
">>> while undobufferentries():\n"
"...     undo()"
msgstr ""
">>> while undobufferentries():\n"
"...     undo()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1585
msgid "Screen methods and functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1587
msgid ""
"Most of the examples in this section refer to a TurtleScreen instance called "
"``screen``."
msgstr ""
"Większość przykładów w tej sekcji odnosi się do instancji TurtleScreen o "
"nazwie ``screen``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1598
msgid "Window control"
msgstr "Kontrola okna"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1604
msgid "Return or set the background color of the TurtleScreen."
msgstr "Zwraca lub ustawia kolor tła TurtleScreen."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1608
msgid "``bgcolor()``"
msgstr "``bgcolor()``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1609
msgid ""
"Return the current background color as a color specification string or as a "
"tuple (see example).  May be used as input to another :func:`color`, :func:"
"`pencolor`, :func:`fillcolor` or :func:`bgcolor` call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1614
msgid "``bgcolor(colorstring)``"
msgstr "``bgcolor(colorstring)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1615
msgid ""
"Set the background color to *colorstring*, which is a Tk color specification "
"string, such as ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"``, or ``\"#33cc8c\"``."
msgstr ""
"Ustawia kolor tła na *colorstring* – jest to specyfikacja koloru w formacie "
"napisu Tk, na przykład ``\"red\"``, ``\"yellow\"`` lub ``\"#33cc8c\"``."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1618
msgid "``bgcolor((r, g, b))``"
msgstr "``bgcolor((r, g, b))``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1619
msgid ""
"Set the background color to the RGB color represented by the tuple of *r*, "
"*g*, and *b*. Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode, "
"where colormode is either 1.0 or 255 (see :func:`colormode`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1624
msgid "``bgcolor(r, g, b)``"
msgstr "``bgcolor(r, g, b)``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1625
msgid ""
"Set the background color to the RGB color represented by *r*, *g*, and *b*. "
"Each of *r*, *g*, and *b* must be between 0 and colormode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1628
msgid ""
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"'orange'\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"#800080\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"(128.0, 0.0, 128.0)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"orange\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"'orange'\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor(\"#800080\")\n"
">>> screen.bgcolor()\n"
"(128.0, 0.0, 128.0)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1641
msgid ""
"a string, name of an image file (PNG, GIF, PGM, and PPM) or ``\"nopic\"``, "
"or ``None``"
msgstr ""
"ciąg znaków, nazwa pliku graficznego (PNG, GIF, PGM i PPM) lub "
"``\"nopic\"``, albo ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1644
msgid ""
"Set background image or return name of current backgroundimage.  If "
"*picname* is a filename, set the corresponding image as background.  If "
"*picname* is ``\"nopic\"``, delete background image, if present.  If "
"*picname* is ``None``, return the filename of the current backgroundimage. ::"
msgstr ""
"Ustawia obraz tła lub zwraca nazwę bieżącego obrazu tła. Jeśli *picname* "
"jest nazwą pliku, ustawia odpowiedni obraz jako tło. Jeśli *picname* to "
"``\"nopic\"``, usuwa obraz tła, o ile istnieje. Jeśli *picname* to ``None``, "
"zwraca nazwę pliku bieżącego obrazu tła. ::"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1649
msgid ""
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"'nopic'\n"
">>> screen.bgpic(\"landscape.gif\")\n"
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"\"landscape.gif\""
msgstr ""
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"'nopic'\n"
">>> screen.bgpic(\"landscape.gif\")\n"
">>> screen.bgpic()\n"
"\"landscape.gif\""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1660
msgid ""
"This TurtleScreen method is available as a global function only under the "
"name ``clearscreen``.  The global function ``clear`` is a different one "
"derived from the Turtle method ``clear``."
msgstr ""
"Ta metoda klasy TurtleScreen jest dostępna jako globalna funkcja wyłącznie "
"pod nazwą ``clearscreen``. Globalna funkcja ``clear`` jest inną funkcją, "
"wywodzącą się z metody ``clear`` klasy Turtle."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1667
msgid ""
"Delete all drawings and all turtles from the TurtleScreen.  Reset the now "
"empty TurtleScreen to its initial state: white background, no background "
"image, no event bindings and tracing on."
msgstr ""
"Usuwa wszystkie rysunki i wszystkie żółwie z ekranu TurtleScreen. Przywraca "
"pusty ekran TurtleScreen do stanu początkowego: białe tło, brak obrazu tła, "
"brak powiązań ze zdarzeniami oraz włączone automatyczne odświeżanie ekranu."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1676
msgid ""
"This TurtleScreen method is available as a global function only under the "
"name ``resetscreen``.  The global function ``reset`` is another one derived "
"from the Turtle method ``reset``."
msgstr ""
"Ta metoda klasy TurtleScreen jest dostępna jako globalna funkcja wyłącznie "
"pod nazwą ``resetscreen``. Globalna funkcja ``reset`` jest inną funkcją, "
"wywodzącą się z metody ``reset`` klasy Turtle."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1683
msgid "Reset all turtles on the screen to their initial state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1688
msgid "positive integer, new width of canvas in pixels"
msgstr "dodatnia liczba całkowita, nowa szerokość płótna w pikselach"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1689
msgid "positive integer, new height of canvas in pixels"
msgstr "dodatnia liczba całkowita, nowa wysokość płótna w pikselach"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1690
msgid "colorstring or color-tuple, new background color"
msgstr "colorstring lub color-krotka, nowy kolor tła"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1692
msgid ""
"If no arguments are given, return current (canvaswidth, canvasheight).  Else "
"resize the canvas the turtles are drawing on.  Do not alter the drawing "
"window.  To observe hidden parts of the canvas, use the scrollbars. With "
"this method, one can make visible those parts of a drawing which were "
"outside the canvas before."
msgstr ""
"Jeśli nie podano argumentów, zwraca aktualne (szerokość płótna, wysokość "
"płótna). W przeciwnym razie zmienia rozmiar płótna, na którym rysują żółwie. "
"Nie zmienia okna rysowania. Aby obejrzeć ukryte części obszaru rysowania, "
"należy użyć pasków przewijania. Za pomocą tej metody można uwidocznić te "
"części rysunku, które wcześniej znajdowały się poza obszarem płótna."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1698
msgid ""
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(400, 300)\n"
">>> screen.screensize(2000,1500)\n"
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(2000, 1500)"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(400, 300)\n"
">>> screen.screensize(2000,1500)\n"
">>> screen.screensize()\n"
"(2000, 1500)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1707
msgid "e.g. to search for an erroneously escaped turtle ;-)"
msgstr "np. aby poszukać żółwia, który przypadkiem uciekł ;-)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1717
msgid ""
"Set up a user-defined coordinate system. *llx* and *lly* are the x and y "
"coordinates of the lower left corner of the canvas. *urx* and *ury* are the "
"x and y coordinates of the upper right corner. Switch to mode \"world\" if "
"necessary, which performs a reset. If mode \"world\" is already active, all "
"drawings are redrawn according to the new coordinates. In user-defined "
"coordinate systems, angles may appear distorted, see :func:`mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1724
msgid ""
">>> screen.reset()\n"
">>> screen.setworldcoordinates(-50,-7.5,50,7.5)\n"
">>> for _ in range(72):\n"
"...     left(10)\n"
"...\n"
">>> for _ in range(8):\n"
"...     left(45); fd(2)   # a regular octagon"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.reset()\n"
">>> screen.setworldcoordinates(-50,-7.5,50,7.5)\n"
">>> for _ in range(72):\n"
"...     left(10)\n"
"...\n"
">>> for _ in range(8):\n"
"...     left(45); fd(2)   # ośmiokąt foremny"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1745
msgid "Animation control"
msgstr "Kontrola animacji"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1749
msgid ""
"Temporarily turn off turtle animation. The code inside the :keyword:`with` "
"block is not animated. Once the block is exited, the drawing appears. This "
"is useful for drawing complex shapes where even the fastest speed setting is "
"too slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1754
msgid ""
">>> with screen.no_animation():\n"
"...     for dist in range(2, 400, 2):\n"
"...         fd(dist)\n"
"...         rt(90)"
msgstr ""
">>> with screen.no_animation():\n"
"...     for dist in range(2, 400, 2):\n"
"...         fd(dist)\n"
"...         rt(90)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1767 ../../library/turtle.rst:1785
#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1786
msgid "a nonnegative integer or ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1769
msgid ""
"Return or set the drawing delay in milliseconds. This is approximately the "
"time interval between two consecutive canvas updates. The longer the drawing "
"delay, the slower the animation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1773
msgid ""
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"10\n"
">>> screen.delay(5)\n"
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"5"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"10\n"
">>> screen.delay(5)\n"
">>> screen.delay()\n"
"5"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1788
msgid ""
"Turn turtle animation on or off and set the drawing delay. If *n* is given, "
"only every n-th regular screen update is performed, which can be used to "
"speed up the drawing of complex graphics. If *n* is 0, animation is turned "
"off and the screen is only updated by calling :func:`update`. If *delay* is "
"given, it sets the drawing delay, see :func:`delay`. When called without "
"arguments, return the current value of *n*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1795
msgid ""
">>> screen.tracer(8, 25)\n"
">>> dist = 2\n"
">>> for i in range(200):\n"
"...     fd(dist)\n"
"...     rt(90)\n"
"...     dist += 2"
msgstr ""
">>> screen.tracer(8, 25)\n"
">>> dist = 2\n"
">>> for i in range(200):\n"
"...     fd(dist)\n"
"...     rt(90)\n"
"...     dist += 2"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1808
msgid "Perform a TurtleScreen update. To be used when tracer is turned off."
msgstr ""
"Wykonuje aktualizację ekranu TurtleScreen. Do użycia, gdy automatyczne "
"odświeżanie ekranu (tracer) jest wyłączone."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1810
msgid "See also the RawTurtle/Turtle method :func:`speed`."
msgstr "Zobacz również metodę :func:`speed` klasy RawTurtle/Turtle."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1814
msgid "Using screen events"
msgstr "Korzystanie ze zdarzeń ekranowych"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1818
msgid ""
"Set focus on TurtleScreen (in order to collect key-events).  Dummy arguments "
"are provided in order to be able to pass :func:`listen` to the onclick "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Ustawia fokus na TurtleScreen, aby umożliwić odbieranie zdarzeń klawiatury. "
"Funkcja przyjmuje dodatkowe, nieużywane argumenty, dzięki czemu funkcję :"
"func:`listen` można przekazać do metody onclick."

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1825 ../../library/turtle.rst:1845
msgid "a function with no arguments or ``None``"
msgstr "funkcja bez argumentów lub ``None``"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1826 ../../library/turtle.rst:1846
msgid "a string: key (e.g. \"a\") or key-symbol (e.g. \"space\")"
msgstr "ciąg znaków: klawisz (np. \"a\") lub symbol klawisza (np. \"space\")"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1828
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to key-release event of key.  If *fun* is ``None``, event "
"bindings are removed. Remark: in order to be able to register key-events, "
"TurtleScreen must have the focus. (See method :func:`listen`.)"
msgstr ""
"Wiąże funkcję *fun* ze zdarzeniem zwolnienia klawisza. Jeśli *fun* ma "
"wartość ``None``, metoda usuwa istniejące powiązania zdarzeń. Uwaga: aby "
"można było rejestrować zdarzenia klawiatury, TurtleScreen musi mieć fokus. "
"(Zobacz metodę :func:`listen`.)"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1832
msgid ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...     lt(60)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkey(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"
msgstr ""
">>> def f():\n"
"...     fd(50)\n"
"...     lt(60)\n"
"...\n"
">>> screen.onkey(f, \"Up\")\n"
">>> screen.listen()"

#: ../../library/turtle.rst:1848
msgid ""
"Bind *fun* to key-press event of key if key is given, or to any key-press-"
"event if no key is given. Remark: in order to be able to register key-"
"events, TurtleScreen must have focus. (See method :func:`listen`.)"
msgstr ""
